{"availability":"available","full":"damianeickhoff/HaCasa","name":"HaCasa","description":"🏠 HaCasa Nova: the HaCasa reboot. A room-first Home Assistant panel, built on the Homio design by iamtherufus.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":473,"forks":51,"created":"2024-01-08T12:14:25Z","updated":"2026-10-08T19:05:56Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://damianeickhoff.github.io/HaCasa/","topics":["custom-panel","dashboard","hacs","home-assistant","homeassistant","homio","lit","lovelace","smart-home"],"demo":"https://damianeickhoff.github.io/HaCasa/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:08.768Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:08.768Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:08.768Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:08.768Z","stars":473,"forks":51}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The HaCasa reboot. A room-first Home Assistant panel, built on the Homio design by iamtherufus.","Documentation · Install · Screenshots · HaCasa v2 (legacy)","HaCasa started as a set of button-card templates: a calm, good-looking dashboard that the whole household could use. It grew to almost 500 stars, and then it stalled, because every new device meant more YAML and every Home Assistant update risked breaking a template."],"features":["Your areas become rooms. Every entity assigned to an area (directly or through its device) shows up on that room's page. Add a lamp in Home Assistant and it appears; no dashboard to edit.","Everything is set up in the panel. A four-step wizard on first open, then a settings page with tabs. Settings are stored per Home Assistant user, so they follow you to every device and survive updates.","No dependencies. No button-card, card-mod, layout-card or theme required."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/damianeickhoff/HaCasa/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a9bc91f31ce593e315ea1d9e2f75b85c3a362cc0b726d63d91d9984c2364532b","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:08.937